{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++ code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++ code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nusing LL = long long;\nconst LL MOD = 1000000007;\n\nstruct Matrix {\n    int N;\n    vector<LL> data;\n    Matrix(int N) : N(N), data(N*N, 0) {\n        for (int i = 0; i < N; ++i) data[i*N+i] = 1;\n    }\n    LL& at(int i, int j) { return data[i*N + j]; }\n    const LL& at(int i, int j) const { return data[i*N + j]; }\n    Matrix operator*(const Matrix& b) const {\n        Matrix r(N);\n        for (int i = 0; i < N; ++i) {\n            for (int j = 0; j < N; ++j) {\n                LL sum = 0;\n                for (int k = 0; k < N; ++k) {\n                    sum = (sum + at(i,k) * b.at(k,j)) % MOD;\n                }\n                r.at(i,j) = sum;\n            }\n        }\n        return r;\n    }\n};\n\nint main() {\n    LL n; int k;\n    cin >> n >> k;\n    int N = k + 1;\n    vector<vector<Matrix>> M(71, vector<Matrix>(31, Matrix(N)));\n    for (int i = 0; i < k; ++i) {\n        M[0][i] = Matrix(N);\n        for (int j = 0; j <= k; ++j) M[0][i].at(i,j) = 1;\n    }\n    vector<LL> kp(100);\n    kp[0] = 1;\n    kp[1] = k;\n    int lg = 2;\n    while (kp[lg-1] <= n / k) {\n        kp[lg] = kp[lg-1] * k;\n        ++lg;\n    }\n    for (int i = 1; i < lg; ++i) {\n        M[i][0] = Matrix(N);\n        for (int j = 1; j < k; ++j) {\n            M[i][j] = M[i-1][j-1] * M[i][j-1];\n        }\n        Matrix cpro(N);\n        for (int j = k-1; j >= 0; --j) {\n            cpro = cpro * M[i-1][j];\n            M[i][j] = M[i][j] * cpro;\n        }\n    }\n    Matrix ans(N);\n    int cc = 0;\n    for (int i = lg-1; i >= 0; --i) {\n        while (kp[i] <= n) {\n            n -= kp[i];\n            ans = M[i][cc] * ans;\n            cc = (cc + 1) % k;\n        }\n    }\n    LL ret = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i <= k; ++i) {\n        ret = (ret + ans.at(i,k)) % MOD;\n    }\n    cout << ret << endl;\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.Scanner;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static final long MOD = 1000000007L;\n\n    static class Matrix {\n        int N;\n        long[] data;\n\n        Matrix(int N) {\n            this.N = N;\n            data = new long[N * N];\n            for (int i = 0; i < N; i++) {\n                data[i * N + i] = 1L;\n            }\n        }\n\n        long get(int i, int j) {\n            return data[i * N + j];\n        }\n\n        void set(int i, int j, long val) {\n            data[i * N + j] = val;\n        }\n\n        Matrix multiply(Matrix b) {\n            Matrix r = new Matrix(N);\n            for (int i = 0; i < N; i++) {\n                for (int j = 0; j < N; j++) {\n                    long sum = 0L;\n                    for (int k = 0; k < N; k++) {\n                        sum = (sum + get(i, k) * b.get(k, j)) % MOD;\n                    }\n                    r.set(i, j, sum);\n                }\n            }\n            return r;\n        }\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner